Step 3 — Generate the Maven web app
bash
cd ~/2026b-cosc2767-a1-<your-repo-name>/question-4
mvn archetype:generate -DgroupId=vn.edu.rmit -DartifactId=my_project -DarchetypeArtifactId=maven-archetype-webapp -DinteractiveMode=false
cd my_project
Step 4 — Force the WAR filename via pom.xml
nano pom.xml

Find the <build> section (it currently just has <finalName>my_project</finalName> or similar, or may need adding). Set it explicitly:

xml
<build>
  <finalName>mywebsite-s123456</finalName>
  ...
</build>

Replace s123456 with your real student ID. This is what controls the actual output filename — the artifactId you set at generation only affects the folder/internal project name, not the packaged file name.

